---
import Article from "../../layouts/Article.astro";
import { go } from "../../data/site";
const toc = [
  { id: "how", label: "How to log in" },
  { id: "google", label: "Google sign-in accounts" },
  { id: "password", label: "Forgot password" },
  { id: "2fa", label: "Two-factor authentication" },
  { id: "issues", label: "Other login problems" },
];
---

<Article
  cover="pocket-option-login"
  title="Pocket Option Login: Sign In and Fix Login Problems"
  description="How to log in to Pocket Option on web and mobile, reset your PocketOption password, use Google sign-in and 2FA, and fix the most common login errors."
  h1="Pocket Option login: fix the most common problems"
  lead="How to sign in on web and mobile, reset your password, and what to do when Google sign-in or two-factor authentication gets in the way."
  crumb="Pocket Option login"
  parent={{ href: "/blog/", label: "Blog" }}
  toc={toc}
  article
  published="2026-11-21"
  updated="2026-11-21"
>
  <h2 id="how">How to log in</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Go to{" "}
      <a href={go("register")} rel="sponsored nofollow">
        Pocket Option
      </a>{" "}
      and press <strong>Log In</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Enter your email and password, or choose <strong>Google</strong> if you registered with it.
    </li>
    <li>Enter your 2FA code if you turned it on.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    On Android, open the app and use the same details. On iPhone, open the web app from your home screen. See{" "}
    <a href="/app/">Pocket Option app</a> for installation.
  </p>

  <h2 id="google">Google sign-in accounts</h2>
  <p>
    If you created your account with Google, it has no password yet. To log in with email and password instead, for
    example on the Telegram bot or a new device, use <strong>Password recovery</strong> with your Google email to set
    one first.
  </p>

  <h2 id="password">Forgot password</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      On the login form, choose <strong>Password recovery</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>Enter your registration email.</li>
    <li>
      Open the link in the email and set a new password. Check your spam folder if it does not arrive within a few
      minutes.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="2fa">Two-factor authentication</h2>
  <p>
    Turn on 2FA in your profile security settings. It adds a one-time code from an authenticator app or email at each
    login. If you lose access to your authenticator, contact support from the login page and be ready to confirm your
    identity.
  </p>

  <h2 id="issues">Other login problems</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Problem</th>
        <th>Fix</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>"Wrong email or password"</td>
        <td>Check for spaces and keyboard language, then reset the password.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Page will not load</td>
        <td>Clear the browser cache, try another browser or switch networks.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Account blocked</td>
        <td>Contact support; blocks usually relate to verification or terms.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Restricted country</td>
        <td>Pocket Option does not serve the EEA, USA, UK, Israel, Japan, the Philippines or Brazil.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="note">
    Only log in at pocketoption.com or the official app. Pages that copy the login form are a common way to steal
    accounts.
  </div>
  <p>
    New to Pocket Option?{" "}
    <a href={go("register")} rel="sponsored nofollow">
      Create an account
    </a>{" "}
    or start on the <a href="/demo-account/">demo</a>.
  </p>
</Article>
